---
title: Burger buns
servings: 8
yield: 8 large buns
tags: [american, fourth of july, summer, vegetarian]
cuisine: american
time: 2 hours 40 minutes
source: Beautiful Burger Buns by King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/beautiful-burger-buns-recipe
---

Knead the @all-purpose flour{420%g}, @water{198%g}(lukewarm), @unsalted butter{28%g}(room temperature), @eggs{1}, @granulated sugar{50%g}, @table salt{1.25%tsp} and @instant yeast{9%g} into a soft, smooth dough.

Cover and leave ~{1%hour} to 2 hours, until nearly doubled.

Deflate it and divide it into 8 pieces of about 100 g. Round each into a ball and flatten it to about 3 inches across.

Set them on a #baking sheet{}, greased or lined with parchment. Cover and leave ~{1%hour}, until clearly puffy. Heat the oven to 375°F (190°C) near the end.

Brush the buns with about half of the @unsalted butter{43%g}(melted). For seeded buns, brush instead with an @egg white{1} whisked with @water{2%tbsp}(cold) and scatter over @sesame seeds{}.

Bake ~{15%minutes} to 18 minutes, until golden. Brush with the rest of the melted butter straight away.

Cool on a #wire rack{} before splitting.

> For 12 smaller buns, use 66 g pieces and bake 12 to 15 minutes. The yolk left
> from the seed wash can go into the dough for colour.
